<description>&lt;p&gt;The junta’s commander Min Aung Hlaing met Japan’s envoy Sasakawa, indicating diplomatic engagement despite ongoing fighting. King Charles III sent books and letters to detained Aung San Suu Kyi, a gesture acknowledged by Myanmar’s government. The conflict continues to generate civilian casualties, with 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP. These diplomatic contacts and royal outreach are new developments compared with the previously reported drone strike on a Chinese gas pipeline and Arakan Army actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQejhmU25UdXc3dUkybk9XcGlYWTdtaGJBQzJ4TEZXdVAzSWt2S192OURVSmtWQmc2dmpCSWw1WVo3X3pYSDFWZlJ5dEhnZUl2THBNdlhQSDJxM2UyNnBDZVFMYUdDbGdHRlBudFdMWGdWX21nbzRHRGQwSFoyYnA0Y1RFaHNRM18xZkluTlVjSFhiWnVfSkRjUGRIT3U0ZW9wY1lZaVJpNHA?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxPYkd3TFJpcjVVOHhyNGhGODVnZzZtNlc5VEFLcVIyMFEyVzY2aGhSOHVKUy1nTTZ0ektqc0ZmN2V6QzZPTjR4SFhTVk9jNWVMY3NhYTdRMjVfZHBGSUNTb0g4ZGN4NWZNMUFNN0oxSm1ZTEhEcEpsSlJpX1M1a1NVYWc3elAwZ1RLcDZpZ3pSZlFlOExxdFUwYzVyMHU4ZVUwc01NZmtiekd6OXBVUmJkTm1vWGd2YUhqaG5XdzlORlA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxPV3dmcEk3N3ZMY1A1WVNEMVNmVkJxbVZmcmhzRkl1eTRKNU9BdmJyWVo0YnpJdW1TU3NueDRyZGlLTGxCT19tVGkzMTFsaF9wVnZOQ05YU0VoNkJsVjFoX2NWdW50Q3Z2WEtxUllYSDNVWll4NmptZEZfU1djdFYtT1RPTS1DTVZaNDA1Z09jdzhvS3dMZHczeWd6anRHLUthRFM5VmMtbUUxZWFWZExPSEVMalROQVZpUjJOdVFXcVlCbUtu?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE90ZThiblBhdHgyb19CTDdHV2Ywb25QdGZkVFhiUnduRFphLWdjTDhMMHNfVURqeE5mN0lBSk1wVGl2UEhla28wWXd5TW8xcGdKWDVTem5LY1hqWVBGeFE?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&q